    "turn_text": "now. Yeah, no 100%. And it is going to be an issue in the campaign, but there are going to be a lot of issues that we discuss. And I'm going to disagree with Representative Cunningham on a lot of issues, but environmental conservation offshore drilling just isn't one of them. And I've stood shoulder to shoulder with him for environmental causes, like being against seismic testing. I have the pictures to prove that I was there. The first piece of legislation I ever filed was an anti-offshore drilling measure. The first rally I ever spoke at on the State House steps was an anti-offshore drilling rally. I stood shoulder to shoulder as the only Republican from the General Assembly with Representative Cunningham when he was first elected to Congress. standing against seismic testing at another rally on the steps of the federal courthouse district court in downtown Charleston. So that's not one of the issues that we're going to disagree on. So I'm not like the previous nominee that had an issue with it. I've consistently been with it. I disagree with him on the approach. I think his approach was very partisan. It wasn't bipartisan. It's never going to become law. It is not law today. Nothing that he's done has moved the ball forward because it'll never pass the U.S. Senate. The president will",
