  {
    "episode_id": 97230,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/7/97230.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 174,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. When my children were very small in 2008, I started my own business. I wanted to be able to be at home with my kids. but also still continue to be able to work. Because I know that sometimes as moms, if you leave the workplace for 10 or 20 years, you don't have the same skills when you come back in, when your kids are older and you're ready to go back to work full time. And so I decided that I am better when I work for myself and started a PR and marketing company doing a lot of B2B work, business to business PR work, mostly in the supply chain, logistics, sort of industry, even trucking. I had a really big client in the trucking industry. And then at that same time met some folks in South Carolina because I'm from there like now Senator Tim Scott and Mick Mulvaney and others that I actually started doing some work for them when they first ran for Congress which was the same year at the same time frame and really fell in love with the political process and seeing what they were doing and trying to do and their message and seeing what it took to actually run for office and when.",
