    "turn_idx": 251,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, well, there's two different issues. There's private property versus public government property. And the Calhoun Monument was on private property. And the owners of the property were OK with it being removed and putting it in the museum if that's where it goes. But I will tell you, burning. burning down a business, destroying a city, tearing down statues and monuments does not do anything to improve the economic and educational circumstances of those communities. It does absolutely zero and all it does is divide the country. What we need to do is really focus on the things that matter. That's education. That's family. That is criminal justice reform and that's prison reform. Those are the kinds of things and we can't do that when we're divided. We can only do that when we get in a room together and listen and work on legislation that Republicans and Democrats together can get behind and move forward.",
