    "turn_text": "job rehabilitating these individuals and giving them hope and giving them jobs and giving them something to live for. And so when we when I see these cities and the violence that's happening when the when the Charleston riots happened at a very good friend of mine beaten unconscious that night. And so, you know, when I see this violence and when I see these businesses being destroyed, people losing their jobs, not only because of COVID, but now because of the writing and businesses, millions of dollars being destroyed, I am passionate about it. This is our town and the low country has always come together. We've always been independent and I want people to know and I want the black community, the African American community, everybody to know that these are things that I've actually worked on. And you have a representative in Congress who hasn't done anything for your communities. I've done it. I've lived it. I've actually passed legislation into law. Had it signed into law. So it is important because it's going on right now.",
