    "turn_idx": 267,
    "turn_text": "I'm going to have to read it and dive into it, but no, we can't go another trillion dollars into debt. We are going to ruin our nation economically and will not be able to come back for it. We had PPP that was doled out to Ivy League universities and big corporations and not to small businesses. We had IEDL that many independent business folks couldn't get. And so, you know, the way that we went about it, the accountability just wasn't there. We had checks going to dead people. Like millions, millions of dollars going to dead people. And you just can't have that. We've got to ensure that we keep our health and safety of our communities, number one, but we've got to keep our economy churning. We've got to allow people who are healthy. You and I have antibodies now, but people who have antibodies and who are healthy and not going to get sick from COVID-19, should be able to work and be able to get jobs and pay their bills, pay their rent, put food on the table and continue on about life as best that they",
