  {
    "episode_id": 97230,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/7/97230.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 287,
    "turn_text": "it's really ugly. And if I do read it, then, you know, I'll get discouraged. I'll get angry. But then it's also the same. At the same time, I'm really passionate. And, you know, and sometimes it is good to hear the other voices, but for an element of folks of the electorate, I will never gonna get their vote, you know? And so that's because of the division that's happening. I could tell you I'm independent until I'm blue in the face, but there's an element of the electorate that will never believe the things that I've done. They just won't believe it. And so, and even some of the slandering that happened when I had COVID-19, it's just so mind-blowing that somebody would say that I knowingly, willfully went in and affected purposefully, the entire first congressional district. I'm like, are you kidding me? Are you like that crazy that anybody would, and their right mind would do that is so crazy to me, but that's where we are in our country right now. That's why this is the election of our lifetime. That's why we have to win this seat back so that we can have real leadership and bring that back to the low country and have someone who's going to put the low country first.",
